.Dd November 24, 2026
.Dt XDIG 1
.Os Belka
.Sh NAME
.Nm xdig
.Nd dig up everything DNS and WHOIS say of a domain
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cPW
.Ar domain | user@domain | url
.Nm
.Fl \-about | \-help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
(eXtended dig) reports on the domain in its argument, which may be a
domain, a mail address, or a URL:
.Bl -bullet
.It
its level, its root domain (its last two labels), and the zone it is
in;
.It
a quick WHOIS of the root domain: its registrar, name servers and
expiry;
.It
the zone's records as they can be seen: SOA, NS, A, AAAA, MX, TXT, CAA
and CNAME, asked for one by one;
.It
what public resolvers (Google, Cloudflare, Quad9) have cached for the
domain, and the zone's serial at each;
.It
where web traffic goes (its addresses) and where mail goes (its MX
hosts' addresses), each with its PTR name and its owner by WHOIS.
.El
.Pp
Queries go to the resolver
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf
names, or to a public resolver directly.
WHOIS starts at whois.iana.org and follows its referrals.
.Pp
The options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
No colour; colour is used only on a terminal.
.It Fl P
Leave out the public resolvers.
.It Fl W
Leave out WHOIS, and so the addresses' owners.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the report is made; 1 if the domain does not exist or is not a
domain; 2 for bad arguments; 111 if there is no resolver.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dig 1 ,
.Xr host 1 ,
.Xr whois 1
.Sh HISTORY
A shell script of 2011, written again in C for Belka, without
.Ql ANY
queries, which servers no longer answer, and with today's public
resolvers.
